{"module": "InterviewGraphBuilder", "question_preview": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "Hello, expert. I'm Amara Okafor, a climate equity and just transition advocate with the Climate Justice and Development Alliance. My work looks at how clean energy and low-carbon technologies affect workers, frontline communities, and developing economies, particularly in Sub-Saharan Africa and South Asia.\n\nTo start, when people talk about the clean energy transition, the story is usually about falling solar and battery costs and record deployment. But those gains aren't reaching everyone equally. **Where do you see the biggest gap between the headline success of clean energy and who is actually benefiting from it?** If you can, please give specific examples, such as particular countries, projects, or financing patterns.", "type": "text"}], "timestamp": "2026-11-10T14:51:41.296109Z", "level": "info", "event": "Question generated successfully"}
